WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.400
A water-restricted mouse starts to drink.

2
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.120
Within a minute, a population of its thirst neurons goes quiet.

3
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.980
Yet five minutes after water access, the salt in its blood is still raised.

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.340
If the brain only corrected errors it had measured in the blood, that could not

5
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:25.120
happen. So what is it responding to?

6
00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:28.733
A homeostatic loop has four parts.

7
00:00:29.453 --> 00:00:34.413
The regulated variable is what is held steady, here plasma osmolality.

8
00:00:35.173 --> 00:00:39.993
A sensor measures it: osmosensitive neurons in the lamina terminalis.

9
00:00:40.593 --> 00:00:44.333
A comparator decides how far it is from where it should be.

10
00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.693
An effector pushes back.

11
00:00:47.673 --> 00:00:51.073
Vasopressin, or AVP, saves water at the kidney.

12
00:00:51.973 --> 00:00:53.173
Thirst takes water in.

13
00:00:53.173 --> 00:00:57.773
The response opposes the error, so this is negative feedback.

14
00:00:59.383 --> 00:01:05.683
A hormone loop has a threshold, where the response starts, and a gain, how much it

15
00:01:05.683 --> 00:01:08.423
grows per unit of error above threshold.

16
00:01:09.483 --> 00:01:15.863
For healthy adults, one summary gives a threshold of 284 milliosmoles per kilogram.

17
00:01:16.663 --> 00:01:22.743
The gain is 0.43 picomoles per liter for each milliozmole per kilogram.

18
00:01:23.423 --> 00:01:25.443
Treat both as illustrative averages.

19
00:01:25.443 --> 00:01:29.323
Below threshold, the line predicts no release.

20
00:01:31.283 --> 00:01:35.523
Take a hypothetical adult on that line, at steady state.

21
00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:40.643
Osmolality is 294, 10 above threshold.

22
00:01:41.723 --> 00:01:43.843
Vasopressin is 4.30.

23
00:01:44.963 --> 00:01:50.403
After drinking, osmolality is 290, and vasopressin is 2.58.

24
00:01:51.003 --> 00:01:55.483
It fell by 1.72. Less error, less hormone.

25
00:01:56.503 --> 00:02:00.123
A pure feedback loop reacts to an error it has measured.

26
00:02:00.967 --> 00:02:06.547
In water-restricted mice, the neurons fall quiet within a minute of drinking.

27
00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:12.007
Seeing water without being allowed to drink does not lower their activity.

28
00:02:12.967 --> 00:02:17.187
In salt-challenged mice, licking an empty bottle does not either.

29
00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:23.247
So something that comes with drinking turns them down, ahead of any change in the

30
00:02:23.247 --> 00:02:29.627
blood. That is feedforward control, a response to a disturbance that is expected.

31
00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:33.647
Researchers put water straight into the stomach.

32
00:02:34.427 --> 00:02:40.887
In hydrated mice, it inhibited the neurons after about 105 seconds, before any

33
00:02:40.887 --> 00:02:43.247
detectable change in blood osmolarity.

34
00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:49.747
Keep the limits. This is a population calcium signal in mice, not the feeling of

35
00:02:49.747 --> 00:02:53.487
thirst. Feedback reacts to a measured error.

36
00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:56.747
Feedforward acts on an expected one.

37
00:02:57.767 --> 00:02:58.827
Thirst uses both.
